ventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HAMAGUCHI SHIGEKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYATAKE NOBUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMORI DAISUKE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKIKAWA KAZUNORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAMAGUCHI, SHIGEKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYATAKE, NOBUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMORI, DAISUKE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKIKAWA, KAZUNORI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A flame retardant for thermoplastic resins which has a toluene insoluble content of 50 wt.% or higher and comprises cross-linked polyorganosiloxane particles having an average particle diameter of 0.01 to 2,000  mu m. Incorporating the flame retardant into a thermoplastic resin gives a flame-retardant resin composition which has excellent impact resistance and generates no harmful gases during burning, i.e., which is friendly to the environment.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne une charge ignifugeante pour résine thermoplastique contenant, d'une part pour au moins 50 % de sa masse un toluène à l'état insoluble, et d'autre part, à l'état réticulé, des particules de polyorganosiloxane d'un diamètre particulaire moyen de 0,01  mu m à 2000  mu m. L'invention concerne également l'incorporation de cette charge ignifugeante dans une composition résine thermoplastique. Le produit obtenu se distingue par une bonne résistance aux chocs ainsi que par l'absence de dégagement de gaz nocifs en cas de combustion, et par conséquent par ses qualités écologiques.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>